    "intent": "teach_concept",
    "title": "How LDR uses pointers",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "kind": "highlight_pdf",
        "targetId": "memory_example",
        "narration": "Start with memory. x4000 is an address; the number 7 is stored there."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "kind": "highlight_pdf",
        "targetId": "pointer_register",
        "narration": "R2 can hold x4000. That means it points at the memory location, not the number 7."
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "kind": "focus_graph",
        "targetId": "pointers",
        "narration": "SmartPath links memory concepts to pointers. Let us focus that idea in the graph."
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "kind": "highlight_pdf",
        "targetId": "ldr_instruction",
        "narration": "LDR R1, R2, #0 uses the address stored in R2, adds zero, and loads the value into R1."
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "kind": "focus_graph",
        "targetId": "ldr",
        "narration": "The LDR node is connected to Pointers in the graph. You are ready for a quick check."
